# playpick cell: mode=walk boss=skyward (coverage label only -- evening steers
# at no boss) spec=paladin:retribution style=dodge size=25 difficulty=heroic
# view=1280x800 save=carried (behaves as fresh, #273).
#
# What is new: this exact spec/style/size/difficulty/save combo already
# produced the deepest zero-wipe evening on record
# (playtest/plans/2026-09-28-29-extended.play, touch 844x390) -- THE VIGIL
# clean, Bonegrinder-heroic clean, Last Whisper taken to 26%. Never tried at a
# desktop/mouse viewport. This script also reuses the short-per-room-budget
# trick 2026-09-27-12.play used to catch a pull honestly `ongoing` (not a wipe
# or a stall) and then presses the corner map button mid-pull -- direction.md's
# still-open "map -> back -> raid erases a live pull's progress" finding, found
# twice on touch (820x1180 and 844x390) and never on a desktop/mouse viewport.
# If the drop reproduces here too, it is confirmed pointer-independent, which
# is the missing axis the existing writeup names as worth checking before the
# gate reopens and it can be filed.
open #b=marrow&s=25&h=1
tap back
tap raid
tap next
tap class:paladin:retribution
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state
evening dodge 60 3
state
shot mid-pull
tap minimap
tap map
state
shot citadel-mid-fight
tap back
state
shot after-back
tap raid
state
shot after-raid-retap
